<p class="eyebrow">BigCommerce connection guide</p><h1>Connect your store with clear control over changes</h1>
<p>BigCommerce is being qualified for a limited customer rollout. Installation is available only to approved stores. A paid StockChief plan and an active BigCommerce store are required. <a href="/pricing">See StockChief pricing</a>; installing an app does not change your subscription.</p>
<h2>Connect and verify</h2>
<ol><li>Sign in to StockChief as the inventory owner. Choose the inventory that should own this store, then open Settings → Connections → BigCommerce.</li>
<li>Enter the store's permanent <code>store-….mybigcommerce.com</code> address. Start Connect and keep the pending window open.</li>
<li>In the same browser, sign in to BigCommerce and review the requested permissions. Complete installation. If the app is unavailable, contact support; a draft app cannot be installed by ordinary customers.</li>
<li>Return to StockChief. Confirm the store identity, then review imported products, variants and locations. Resolve ambiguous matches before enabling write-back.</li>
<li>Check the last successful catalog check and event status. A connected account alone does not prove that events or outgoing changes have been delivered.</li></ol>
<h2>Choose stock and price synchronization</h2>
<p>On the connection page, open <strong>Set up stock and price synchronization</strong>. Enter one exact mapped SKU and location. Choose a direction for stock and price separately: StockChief to provider, provider to StockChief, both directions, or off. Leave unchanged preserves the existing setting.</p>
<p>If starting values differ, choose the source you intend to trust, or leave <strong>Stop and ask me</strong> selected. Select <strong>Review synchronization</strong>, inspect the current values and exact matches, then approve the proposed change. No ongoing write-back starts merely from installing the app or opening this form.</p>
<p>Outgoing quantity is costed, uncommitted stock available to sell. Physical stock without cost evidence may therefore publish as zero. Incoming count differences need physical confirmation; they do not establish purchases, costs or returns. Do not enter invented costs to make a test pass.</p>
<p>A delivery is complete only when StockChief reads the resulting value back from BigCommerce. Queued, pending or uncertain deliveries are not verified. Conflicting values pause for review.</p>
<h2>Recover without repeating a change</h2>
<ul><li>If consent was cancelled or expired, start a fresh Connect request from StockChief. Do not reuse an old callback URL.</li>
<li>If a result page is blocked or closes, inspect the connection's actual status before submitting again. An action may have completed.</li>
<li>If authorization is revoked, use Reconnect as the current inventory owner. Never paste tokens or client secrets into chat or support messages.</li>
<li>To stop outgoing changes, set the affected stock and price directions to Off and review the proposal. Verify that both show Off before making manual provider corrections.</li>
<li>Uninstalling the app revokes its connection. Existing inventory and accounting history are retained; uninstall does not reverse previously approved business changes.</li></ul>
<h2>Current scope</h2>
<p>The owned-store pilot verified catalog import, a live product-change event, a guarded stock decrease and price write-back with read-back. Broader customer onboarding, positive costed stock, variant/location combinations and live order/refund workflows require their own qualification. No multi-storefront, multi-location or Catalyst badge is claimed by this guide.</p>
<p>For help, <a href="/support?topic=help">contact StockChief support</a> or email <a href="mailto:support@stockchiefhq.com">support@stockchiefhq.com</a>. Include the store name, approximate time and visible error, without credentials or customer records.</p>
